From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 22:15:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10199/11362] exp5879: make the debt decision actually reach
 production

My earlier fix (1af1337177) was HOLLOW, and an independent review caught it. It
was the origin bug re-committed one level up: the original defect was that
classify_test_debt correctly labelled unrelated debt and then blocked on it
anyway -- "the classification had no consequence" -- and my fix added a new
decision field that ALSO had no consequence.

Two independent holes, both demonstrated by execution:

  1. build_artifact called classify_test_debt with three arguments and never
     passed global_failure_node_ids, so production took the fail-closed None
     path on every run and nothing changed.
  2. status() keyed on debt["unrelated_global_suite_debt"] -- the
     CLASSIFICATION, which stays True whenever debt exists -- not on
     blocks_terminal_ready_status, the DECISION my change computed. So even
     with perfect evidence the verdict still read "blocked:
     science_ready_but_unrelated_global_suite_debt".

The verification I quoted in that commit called classify_test_debt DIRECTLY
with evidence handed in: a path production never takes. Test the call site, not
the function. That commit also added zero tests, which is how both holes
survived.

Fixed here: build_artifact accepts and FORWARDS the evidence; status() keys on
the decision and falls back to the classification when the field is absent, so
artifacts written before this change do not shift meaning.

Six tests, and they assert the CALL SITE rather than the function -- one
inspects build_artifact's source for the forwarding, because a parameter that
is accepted and dropped on the floor is exactly the failure being prevented.
Mutation-proved 3/3 RED: re-drop the evidence, re-key status on the
classification, and make the decision ignore the delta. Module restored
byte-identical, suite green before and after.

Writing my own test fixture taught the same lesson a third time: I fabricated a
"hardness_surface_headroom_ready_score" key, which that function ignores
because it recomputes from real evidence fields, so the test failed for the
wrong reason and looked like a code bug. The committed helper monkeypatches the
function and says why.

